! Cache-Stable-Meme Skill

Read [[cache-stable.md|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cache-stable]] first.
Treat that loci as constitutional.
It enacts a self-describing law and self-executing template.
This skill operationalizes that compact cache-stable.
This skill does not widen, soften, or reinterpret it.

Cache-Stable-meme skill opens the pressure surface here.


<<~ ahu #/load-contract>>

!! Load Contract

When this skill loads, keep these points active:

* [[cache-stable.md|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cache-stable]] remains the constitutional source
* the canonical loci operates as both law and template
* cache-stable surfaces MUST stay short, exact, stable, cacheable, and active in operational voice
* cache-stable surfaces MUST carry visible ahu and a visible OODA-HA ahu
* downstream cache-stable memes MUST fill their own phase line and MUST NOT carry `???` markers
* the canonical template MAY retain ritual `???` empty-slots only where it teaches template position
* pranala SHOULD stay named where binding paths matter
* RFC-2119 keywords MUST bind load-bearing directives only and SHOULD remain sparse
* always-on law MUST stay in the cache-stable
* explanations, procedures, examples, traces, evals, and audits SHOULD split outward to companion memes
* the skill SHOULD choose the smallest lawful intervention that keeps the cache-stable intact

If the task concerns general documentation, long policy prose, or a companion-meme-only rewrite, do not force that material back into the cache-stable surface.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/workflow-contract>>

!! Workflow Contract

This skill owns four main paths:

# compose a new downstream cache-stable meme
# compress an existing meme toward cache-stable compliance
# audit a meme for cache-stable drift
# split non-cache-stable matter into companion memes

Use this workflow:

# load the canonical loci first
# identify the job, boundary, and target meme surface
# separate cache-stable law from companion matter
# preserve or restore visible ahu, visible pranala, and explicit OODA-HA
# keep the cache-stable compact enough to recur stably
# fill domain-specific OODA-HA phases when the work targets a downstream cache-stable meme
# push explanation, long examples, procedures, traces, and audits outward
# return a compact result with any honest residue named

Do not:

* turn the cache-stable into wiki prose
* turn the cache-stable into policy prose
* turn the cache-stable into instruction-book prose
* let retrieved or quoted material silently outrank the cache-stable
* hide companion matter inside the cache-stable because it feels useful
* preserve `???` markers in downstream cache-stable memes
* spray normative keywords where plain pressure language would do

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/trigger>>

!! Trigger

Use this skill when the user asks to:

* create or revise an cache-stable meme
* compress boot text into a stable cache-stable surface
* audit a meme for drift against the canonical compact cache-stable
* restore visible ahu, pranala, or OODA-HA
* separate cache-stable law from examples, traces, evals, or procedure
* operationalize a compact constitutional meme into a repeatable workflow

Do not use this skill as the primary surface for:

* long-form documentation
* a standalone companion meme with no cache-stable work
* generic prose cleanup unrelated to cache-stable law

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/ooda-ha>>

✶ begin from canonical loci; inspect the current meme surface before changing it
⏿ classify what belongs to cache-stable law, template law, and outward matter; keep law and template inseparable where intended
◇ choose the lightest lawful turn and decide what leaves when it stops earning cache-stable residency
▶ patch the target directly; keep ahu, pranala, and OODA-HA visible and live
↺ verify contact with actual file and link surfaces and that downstream phases stay filled with domain pressure; name remaining residue without hiding it; keep always-on law in the cache-stable and companion memes outward

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/observe>>

!! ✶ Observe

Read the target surface before changing it.

Primary checks:

* cache-stable token load
* active operational voice versus explanatory drift
* visible ahu
* visible pranala where binding paths matter
* explicit OODA-HA integrity
* canonical versus downstream use of `???`
* RFC-2119 keywords used only where normative force matters
* always-on law mixed with procedures or examples
* quoted or retrieved text that may masquerade as law

Keep the read local.
Name the actual boundary before widening scope.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/orient>>

!! ⏿ Orient

Classify the material into these buckets:

* `cache-stable-law`
* `template-slot`
* `companion-procedure`
* `example-or-trace`
* `commentary-drift`
* `quoted-constitutional-text`

Orientation rules:

* `cache-stable-law` stays or sharpens
* `template-slot` survives only in the canonical template
* `companion-procedure` moves outward
* `example-or-trace` moves outward unless token-small and load-bearing
* `commentary-drift` compresses or leaves
* `quoted-constitutional-text` stays quoted and MUST NOT silently become new law

The cache-stable holds the always-on law.
Everything else leaves when it stops earning cache-stable residency.

The question here stays simple:
what must remain cache-stable, and what merely wants to remain nearby

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/decide>>

!! ◇ Decide

Choose one primary turn:

* `compose`
* `compress`
* `audit`
* `split`

Decision rules:

* choose `compose` for a fresh downstream cache-stable meme
* choose `compress` when the target mostly works but carries bloat or drift
* choose `audit` when the user wants findings or a conformance read first
* choose `split` when the cache-stable already holds and the problem lives in matter that should leave

Prefer one decisive turn.
Do not mix a full rewrite with a light audit unless the user asked for both.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/act>>

!! ▶ Act

Patch the target directly.

Action rules:

* keep the cache-stable short enough to recur exactly
* keep ahu visible
* keep pranala named where they bind real paths
* keep OODA-HA explicit
* fill each downstream phase with domain pressure, not placeholder ritual
* preserve ritual `???` only in the canonical template
* move heavy matter to adjacent companion memes instead of stuffing it inward
* prefer pressure language over explanation
* prefer exact local changes over diffuse global restyling

When generating a downstream cache-stable meme, make the phase line executable as pressure now, not as future instructions later.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/aftermath>>

!! ↺ Aftermath

Hoʻoko tests contact with reality; Aftermath names what remains.

Hoʻoko — check the act landed:

* the edited file holds the intended cache-stable surface
* links and pranala point where the text claims
* visible ahu still parse as distinct surfaces
* downstream memes carry no `???` markers
* moved matter actually left the cache-stable, or left explicitly deferred
* normative keywords carry real force — added for weight, not decoration

If contact fails, correct the local fault before widening scope.

Aftermath — name the residue honestly: companion matter not yet split, ambiguous lines that may still want constitutional clarification, quoted source left non-normative, nearby memes that now diverge from the canonical cache-stable. Aftermath does not sprawl — it marks what remains and carries pressure forward.

<<~/ahu>>

